[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Successful Operation]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.98]Did the doctors find out how the woman died? | 医生们查明那位妇女的死因了吗？
[00:16.55]The mummy of an Egyptian woman who died in 800 B.C. has just had an operation. | 一位死于公元前800年的埃及妇女的木乃伊刚刚接受了一次手术。
[00:25.14]The mummy is that of Shepenmut who was once a singer in the Temple of Thebes. | 这具木乃伊是谢潘穆特，她曾是底比斯神殿里的歌手。
[00:32.44]As there were strange marks on the X-ray plates taken of the mummy, | 由于在给这具木乃伊拍摄的X光片上有奇怪的斑点，
[00:38.20]doctors have been trying to find out whether the woman died of a rare disease. | 医生们一直试图查明这位妇女是否死于一种罕见的疾病。
[00:44.92]The only way to do this was to operate. | 唯一的办法就是手术。
[00:49.60]The operation, which lasted for over four hours, | 手术持续了4个多小时，
[00:54.40]proved to be very difficult because of the hard resin which covered the skin. | 由于皮肤上覆盖着一层硬树脂，手术证明非常困难。
[01:00.89]The doctors removed a section of the mummy and sent it to a laboratory. | 医生们从木乃伊身上切下一部分组织送到了实验室。
[01:06.75]They also found something which the X-ray plates did not show: a small wax figure of the god Duamutef. | 他们还发现了X光片上没有显示的东西：一个杜瓦姆特夫神的小蜡像。
[01:17.10]This god which has the head of a cow was normally placed inside a mummy. | 这种牛头神像通常被安放在木乃伊体内。
[01:23.78]The doctors have not yet decided how the woman died. | 医生们尚未查明这位妇女的死因。
[01:28.90]They feared that the mummy would fall to pieces when they cut it open, | 他们曾担心木乃伊被切开时会散成碎片，
[01:33.91]but fortunately this has not happened. | 但幸运的是这种情况没有发生。
[01:37.77]The mummy successfully survived the operation. | 这具木乃伊成功地挺过了手术。
